---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StructuredData from '../components/StructuredData.astro';
import BookBlock from '../components/BookBlock.astro';

const title = 'Fourth Wing Gift Ideas: By Recipient, Budget and Timing';
const description = 'Gift ideas for Fourth Wing fans, organized by who you are buying for, how much you want to spend, and whether you need it before the holidays.';
const faqs = [
  { question: 'What do you get someone who loves Fourth Wing?', answer: 'It depends on how far they have read. For a new reader, bookmarks, stickers or a mug assume no plot knowledge. For someone who has finished the books, a hardcover or special edition, a reading journal, or something for their shelf is more likely to be new to them.' },
  { question: 'What is a good Fourth Wing gift under $25?', answer: 'Bookmarks, sticker sets, pins and a single mug are the categories that most often fall in that range. Prices change by seller, so compare on the listing page.' },
  { question: 'Is Fourth Wing merchandise officially licensed?', answer: 'Some of it is, and some is fan-made. Several stores describe their Fourth Wing lines as officially licensed, and the author runs her own shop. Check the label on the product page; our merchandise guide explains the difference.', linked: true },
  { question: 'Are there Fourth Wing gifts that do not need shipping?', answer: 'Yes — ebooks, audiobooks and bookstore gift cards are delivered digitally and are the safe option if you are buying close to the date.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Fourth Wing Gift Ideas', href: '/fourth-wing-gift/' }]}>
  <h1>Fourth Wing Gift Ideas: By Recipient, Budget and Timing</h1>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="lead">Buying for a Fourth Wing reader is mostly a question of how far into the series they
      are, and how much you want to spend. This page is organized by those two things.
      We do not sell these items — we link to sellers.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="before-you-buy">
      <h2 id="before-you-buy">Three Things to Check Before You Buy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>How far they have read. The series is still being published, and merchandise often
          carries artwork or quotes from later books. If you are not sure how far they have got,
          choose something that does not reference specific events.</li>
        <li>Sizing. Apparel is the largest category and the only one where a wrong guess cannot be
          fixed. If you do not know their size, drinkware, bookmarks or stationery carry no sizing
          risk.</li>
        <li>Licensed or fan-made. Both are widely sold and both are easy to find. For a gift, the
          label on the product page is what tells you which one you are buying — the difference is
          explained on our merchandise guide.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="new-readers">
      <h2 id="new-readers">Gifts for Someone Who Just Started the Series</h2>
      <p>The safest gifts for a new reader are the ones that do not assume any knowledge of the
        plot: bookmarks, stickers, a tote, a mug. Anything with character art or a quote assumes
        they have met that character already. Bookish accessories also work if they read widely,
        not just this series.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="caught-up-readers">
      <h2 id="caught-up-readers">Gifts for Someone Who Has Read Everything</h2>
      <p>Once someone has finished the published books, the useful gifts shift from accessories
        to objects: a nicer edition of a book they already own, a reading journal, or something
        for their shelf rather than their bag. This is also the group most likely to already own
        the common items, so a specific, narrow gift tends to land better than a general one.</p>
      <BookBlock headingLevel="h3" labelAffiliate />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="budget">
      <h2 id="budget">Gifts by Budget</h2>
      <p>Prices move constantly and vary by seller, so the bands below describe what kind of item
        usually falls where — check the listing for the actual number.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table aria-label="Gift budget bands">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Band</th><th scope="col">What usually sits here</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Under $25</th><td>Bookmarks, sticker sets, pins, a single mug</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">$25–$50</th><td>Apparel, a hoodie or sweatshirt, a candle or blanket</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Over $50</th><td>A hardcover or special edition, a bundle, a larger gift set</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>If you are buying for a gift exchange with a fixed limit, bookmarks and sticker sets are
        the categories that most often stay under $25.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="timing">
      <h2 id="timing">Will It Arrive in Time?</h2>
      <p>Two things affect timing, and only one of them is shipping.
        The first is stock: popular sizes and designs in this fandom sell out in December, and a
        listing that is available in November may not be in December.
        The second is format: ebooks and audiobooks are delivered instantly and need no shipping
        at all, which makes them the reliable last-minute option. Gift cards for a bookstore
        chain work the same way.</p>
      <p>If you are buying within a week of the date, choose a format that is delivered
        digitally rather than a physical item.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="faq">
      <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <dl>{faqs.map(({ question, answer, linked }) => <div class="faq-item">
        <dt><strong>{question}</strong></dt>
        <dd>{linked ? <>Some of it is, and some is fan-made. Several stores describe their Fourth Wing lines as
          officially licensed, and the author runs her own shop. Check the label on the product page;
          our merchandise guide explains the difference.</> : answer}</dd>
      </div>)}</dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="related-pages">
      <h2 id="related-pages">Related Pages</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/fourth-wing-merchandise/">Fourth Wing Merchandise: Official Stores and Fan-Made Picks</a></li>
        <li><a href="/fourth-wing-characters/">Fourth Wing Characters</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/threshing/">What Threshing Day Is</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="affiliate-disclosure purchase-disclosure">As an Amazon Associate and Etsy Affiliate, I earn from qualifying purchases. Links marked as affiliate earn
      a commission; links to official stores do not. Prices and availability change — the
      listing page is the source of truth.</p>
  </article>
  <StructuredData data={{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqs.map(({ question, answer }) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: question, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: answer } })) }} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  li + li { margin-top: .8rem; }
  .faq-item { padding: 1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); line-height: 1.75; }
  .affiliate-disclosure { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: .875rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
